# Canonical pins for this repo's Dockerfile. Bump via scripts/bump-pin.sh.
# Last updated: 2026-05-06 (Wave 10: full cu13 stack migration)
DEEPEP_FORK=https://github.com/dmvevents/DeepEP-1.git
DEEPEP_BRANCH=aws-efa-auto-qp-cap-v2
DEEPEP_SHA=146cc356aa00c39ac1590c05775e05b0f031e70c

# Wave 10: unified cu13 stack to resolve Wave 9c finding that cu12 NCCL
# wheels do NOT expose the DeepEP V2 GIN ABI (ncclTeamWorld,
# ncclCommProperties, etc.) that csrc/kernels/backend/nccl.cu calls.
# cu13 NCCL wheels DO expose those symbols, and cu13 also resolves
# Wave 8's invalid-device-ordinal crash caused by two libcudart.so
# copies (torch cu12 + vllm _C.abi3.so cu13) racing on TLS.
#
# Per god-mode 3-model consensus 2026-05-06 (Option 3: flip every
# runtime component to cu13). Build OS remains cu12.9-devel because
# nvidia/cuda:13.0-devel-ubuntu24.04 is not yet on Docker Hub
# (verified 2026-05-06); cu13 runtime components land via pip wheels.
#
# NOTE: the value MUST be single-quoted because `>=` would otherwise
# be interpreted as shell redirection when pins.env is sourced
# (regression seen in a failed v0.1.2-sm90a GHA run).
NVIDIA_NCCL_PIN='nvidia-nccl-cu13>=2.30.4'

# PyTorch index URL. Wave 10 originally targeted cu130 but hit a
# blocker: NVIDIA has NOT yet published cu13 developer toolkit wheels
# to PyPI (nvidia-cuda-nvcc-cu13 == 0.0.1 placeholder, verified
# 2026-05-06) and Docker Hub has NOT yet published
# nvidia/cuda:13.0-devel-ubuntu24.04. Without a cu13 nvcc the torch
# cpp_extension check `cuda_ver.major != torch_cuda_version.major`
# raises `RuntimeError: detected CUDA version (12.9) mismatches the
# version that was used to compile PyTorch (13.0)` and DeepEP's
# `pip install -e .` cannot build its CUDAExtensions.
#
# Resolution (Wave 10 retry 1): torch stays on cu129 to match the
# cu12.9-devel base image's nvcc, but the NCCL pip wheel flips to
# cu13 via `--no-deps --upgrade`. cu12 NCCL 2.30.4 DOES export
# `ncclTeamWorld` (verified 2026-05-06 via `nm -D` on the downloaded
# wheel: `000000000018e430 W ncclTeamWorld`) BUT does NOT export
# `ncclCommProperties` which DeepEP V2 csrc/kernels/backend/nccl.cu
# calls. cu13 NCCL does export it. Using cu13 NCCL under cu129 torch
# gives us the DeepEP-required ABI without blocking on cu13 toolkit
# availability. This is the Wave 9 cu12 stack + cu13 NCCL override,
# not the full cu13 unification that god-mode recommended (blocked).
TORCH_INDEX=https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu129
